n\u2019t have 4 melds + pair yet. Let\u2019s check if current grouping is possible:  \n\nMeld1: B8 pung.  \nPossible meld2: J2 pung (J2 J2 J2).  \nPossible meld3: B7 pung (B7 B7 B7).  \nThen remaining: W4, W8, T5 T5, T8, T9, F1.  \nNeed 1 meld + 1 pair from these 6 tiles.  \nPair could be T5 T5 (then meld from W4, W8, T8, T9, F1 impossible), or pair F1+? (only 1 F1), or pair W4+? (only 1 W4), etc. Not working.  \n\nMaybe sequence melds:  \nMeld1: B8 pung.  \nMeld2: T8 T9 + T7 (not in hand).  \nMeld3: T5 T6 T7 (not in hand).  \nSo not tenpai. We must discard 1 tile to get to 13 tiles (since meld is fixed, hand must be 10 tiles after discard to be in 13 total).  \n\nSo we are not in tenpai yet \u2014 need to discard 1 tile now from valid actions to improve toward tenpai.  \n\n---\n\n**Evaluation of discard options:**  \n\nHand: W4, W8, T5 T5, T8, T9, B7 B7, F1, J2 J2.  \nPotential good shapes:  \n- J2 pair is safe (J2 seen 2 in hand, 4 total in game, 2 left unseen maybe).  \n- B7 pair also possible.  \n- T5 pair possible.  \n\nWe have isolated honors: F1 (wind), J2 (dragon). J2 already pair, maybe keep for pair.  \nSuits: W (W4, W8 disconnected), T (T5 T5, T8, T9), B (B7 B7).  \n\nT shape: T5 T5 T8 T9 \u2014 can form T5 T6 T7 sequence if we get T6 T7, or T7 T8 T9 if we get T7, or T5 T5 T5 pung if we get T5. T8 T9 needs T7. T5 pair is okay.  \n\nB shape: B7 B7 only.  \n\nWe want to move toward tenpai with flexibility and value.  \n\nPossible discards:  \n- F1: isolated wind, safe discard (F1 seen 1 in hand, 4 total in game, 3 left unseen \u2014 but prevalent wind North F4, seat wind East F1, so F1 is seat wind \u2014 discard seat wind may be risky for others to pung, but no F1 in others\u2019 melds, maybe safe).  \n- W4, W8: isolated, but W4 connects to W3 W5, W8 connects to W7 W9, but we have none of those.  \n- T9: leaves T5 T5 T8, needs T6 T7 or T7 T9? Not good.  \n- T8: leaves T5 T5 T9, needs T6 T7 or T4 T5 T6?  \n\nBest is to keep T8 T9 together (potential T7 wait) and T5 T5 (potential pung or T4 T6 sequence).  \n\nB7 B7 could become pung if we get 1 more B7 (only 1 left unseen \u2014 B7: total 4, 2 in hand, 1 in prev player\u2019s meld [B5 B6 B7], so 1 left).  \n\nSo:  \nIf we discard W4 or W8, we keep T shape intact and B7 B7, J2 J2, F1.  \n\nBut F1 is a terminal/honor, could help Pung of Terminals or Honors (1 point) if we get 2 more, unlikely. Discard F1 first.  \n\nJ2 is dragon, already pair, maybe keep for possible Two Dragon Pungs if we get J1 or J3 pung.  \n\nSo promising discards: F1, then W4, W8.  \n\nCheck safety:  \nF1: 4 total, 1 in hand, none in others\u2019 melds, 3 unseen. Could be dangerous for others to win if they need seat wind, but less likely.  \nW4: 3 left unseen, connects to W3 W5, but not too dangerous.  \n\nGiven scoring potential:  \nWe have B8 pung already (no pattern unless All Simples maybe, but B8 is simple).  \nIf we aim for All Types (contains all 3 suits + winds + dragons), we have W, T, B, F, J already in hand, so possible.  \n\nSo keep one of each suit and honors. Discard W4 or W8? W4 is more central but dead here.  \n\nBetter: discard W8 (more isolated than W4? both isolated). Actually W4 can connect to W3 W5 (both 3 unseen each), W8 connects to W7 (1 unseen) W9 (2 unseen). So W4 slightly better to keep? But both bad.  \n\nGiven opponents\u2019 discards:  \nNext player meld: T2 pung.  \nAcross: F3 pung, W2 W3 W4 chow.  \nPrevious: B5 B6 B7 chow, B1 B2 B3 chow.  \n\nPrevious player likely has hand with sequences, maybe near ready. Dangerous tiles: B4? B8?  \n\nWe need safe tile. F1 might be safe from previous player because they have no F1 meld, but seat wind could be needed for hand.  \n\nBut given game phase (many melds already), maybe safer to discard F1.  \n\n---\n\n**Evaluation:**  \nF1 is the most useless honor here (only 1 copy, no sequence value, keeping it doesn\u2019t help much except for All Types, but we already have F in hand via none? Actually F1 is only F, so discard F1 loses All Types? Wait All Types needs W, T, B, F, J. If we discard F1, we have no F tile, so All Types impossible. So maybe keep F1 for All Types chance.  \n\nThen discard W4 or W8. W4 more likely to be dangerous? W4 is in across player\u2019s chow (W2 W3 W4), so they have W4 already, safe to discard W4. Yes, W4 is safer.  \n\nSo discard W4.  \n\n---\n\n**Reason:**  \nW4 is seen in across player\u2019s meld, so safe from giving them extra win chance. Keeps F1 for possible All Types pattern, keeps T shape for sequences, keeps B7 pair and J2 pair options. Best step toward tenpai without giving dangerous tile.  \n\n---\n\n**Answer:** Play W4"}
